    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d633">

                <pb facs="0753" n="693" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg693"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Sir
                            Julian Pauncefote</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-28"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 304.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that
                    your notes dated the 16th, 19th, and 24th instant, respectively, in relation to
                    the shooting <pb facs="0754" n="694" xml:id="pg694"/> of Mr. James Bain, purser
                    of the British steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Engineer</hi>, have been
                    received, and copies thereof sent to the governor of Louisiana for his
                    information.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
